notes: "The usual explanation is AI style — a font, a gradient, a layout. I don't think that's it. The deck I recognized was complete in a way a person rarely is. Every point had a slide; every slide had a heading; every heading had three bullets. Completeness was the problem. A person makes a deck by deciding what not to say. The left page is a real page from this deck that tries to cover every point; the right is a Section divider that chooses one pause. The difference is not decoration; it is focus."
